WEBVTT

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.100
I'm going back to the majors?!

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.470
The manager of the Hornets gave me a call this morning.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.690
If you do well in today's game, he wants you back immediately.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.950
All right!

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.960
However,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:19.640
you must pitch at least seven innings with no runs or walks as the starting pitcher.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.200
Not so easy, is it?

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:24.870
Strike!

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.760
His pitches are all fast pitches to the corners.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.050
Still, he's not the same as he was in the World Cup.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.010
Ball.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.430
Am I getting used to his pitching?

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.340
No, that's not it.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:47.520
When I struck out at the World Cup, I was overwhelmed by devastation.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.930
He doesn't have that overwhelming presence anymore.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.130
Safe! Safe!

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.760
Oh man, they got a run.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:29.020
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:29.020
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:34.320
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:34.320
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.700
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.700
the only thing I truly have

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:45.000
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:45.000
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.330
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.330
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:55.590
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:55.590
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:00.970
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:00.970
I had begun to understand many things

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:07.060
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:07.060
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.610
garakuta no yama kara

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.610
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.690
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.690
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:21.990
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:21.990
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:28.290
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:28.290
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:33.920
namida kareru made

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:33.920
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.970
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.970
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:44.310
namida hareru made

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:44.310
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:49.310
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:49.310
though I may lose my way,

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.150
egakikake no ima

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.150
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.650
kizamu

00:02:53.150 --> 00:03:00.400
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.940
akashi

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.400
kono te de

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:06.160
What it Takes to be a Pro

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:06.160
What it Takes to be a Pro

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:14.610
Now hitting, number 5: Edwards!

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:21.050
With one out and a runner on second, the fourth batter, Edwards, is at bat.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.760
This is the real test.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.180
If you can't get through this, your yips will come right back, Shigeno.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.350
Ball.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.080
Calm down.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.940
That pitch wasn't bad.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.450
Silva got lucky, that's all.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:50.090
I can't go back to the majors now that I've given up a run,

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:54.130
but this doesn't mean I won't have another chance.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.710
Just let it go.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.630
You're an idiot if you mess up your rhythm by worrying about every pitch.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.940
The end result is all that matters for professionals.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.240
Out!

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:24.850
Out!

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:26.820
Three outs. Change!

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:32.410
Even after Silva's RBI, Shigeno held his ground and ended the inning.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.150
Okay, that was good.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:45.680
You couldn't hold seven innings down without a run, but you didn't let it get to you.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.600
Thanks.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:53.970
If you continue to prove yourself like today, you'll definitely go back to the majors.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.550
You can hit the showers if you want.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:57.400
What do you say?

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:02.530
All right, I'll head off and get ready for the next game.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.860
Okay.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:08.340
Nice pitching today.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.000
Nice pitching.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.460
Get some rest, Shigeno.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.410
You pitched well.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.900
Hey, Shigeno!

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.430
Let's go grab a bite to eat.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.230
Butler's paying since he got four RBIs.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.910
No, maybe some other time.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:37.990
Really?

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:38.890
That's a pity.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.190
Well, see ya.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.530
Something's not right...

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.730
I'm not frustrated about Silva's hit,

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.500
but I'm not excited that I didn't break down.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.300
What's gotten into me?

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.380
Well, you're looking kind of down.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.840
Silva!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:07.730
What's up?

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:13.260
I heard you're in the minors because of the yips.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:17.100
You really don't look that weak,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.270
but I guess you are.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.020
What was that?!

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.400
You here to make fun of me?

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.610
Don't get on some high horse from a lucky hit!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:26.940
Geez!

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.280
Luck?

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.800
You seriously think it was luck?

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.720
Looks like you won't be back in the majors for a while.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.460
Wh-What?

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.870
Sorry about that.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:48.760
I didn't come here to pick a fight.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:58.060
I just don't understand why you're like this after you decimated our Venezuelan team...

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:03.020
and pitched like crazy against the American sluggers.

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:07.420
If you can't keep it together in critical situations like today,

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.300
no one will be afraid of you.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.180
If you play like that, you're going to need a lot of luck to win in the majors.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.590
I'm going back to the majors tomorrow.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:20.140
I hope I see you there soon.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.190
Hello.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.940
Shigeno?

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.100
It's Alice.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:48.530
I just got a call from the manager of the Hornets.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.700
Congratulations, you're a major leaguer again!

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.480
Wait, wh-what?

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:57.870
Silva got a run off me, so how's that...?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:04.770
That was just so you'd be under pressure, so they could see if you'd conquered the yips.

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:12.360
Since you could still pitch fine after that run, he said you'll probably be fine.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:17.830
Is something wrong?

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:18.850
Aren't you happy?

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.540
W-Well...

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.740
Of course I am.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.270
I just wasn't expecting this.

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:28.180
I see.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.370
Good luck.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.010
Make sure I never see you here again, okay?

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.150
Thanks.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.010
Hey.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:56.930
Still alive and kicking, huh?

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.500
Hey, stop!

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:03.040
Hey...

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.370
Why'd you come back?

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:08.440
I thought you went back to the majors in Indianapolis.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:11.990
Yeah, I'm going right now.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:14.410
The taxi's waiting right there.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:18.600
I just wanted to thank you before I left.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:28.030
I never thought I'd get over the yips and be back to the majors so quickly.

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.130
I'm really grateful.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:33.340
All I did was give you normal counseling sessions.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:38.390
It was your strong heart that helped you recover so quickly.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:40.440
You're impressive.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:47.980
Am I really fixed, Dr. Oliver?

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:50.400
What do you mean?

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:54.320
Silva told me something yesterday.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:10:01.200
He said that I've become a boring pitcher who can't keep it together when it matters.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:05.460
I can see it myself.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:11.420
I can try to pitch calmly and with fewer risks,

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:13.310
but...

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:19.760
I can't get the adrenaline flowing like I used to.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:29.410
Perhaps I haven't done enough to completely cure you.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:33.210
This is just a theory,

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:37.620
but I think your yips comes from more than just Gibson Jr.'s hit.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:41.200
I think there's a deeper, underlying reason.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.860
A deeper reason?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:45.870
Gibson.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.160
Gibson?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:54.380
Gibson has long been your goal,

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.880
and even your symbol of baseball.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:02.710
After so many years you were finally able to pitch alongside him, but now that he's retired...

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:06.810
No, that problem's already been resolved.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:13.610
After hearing that Gibson retired, I lost all my will to play baseball...

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.480
because I wouldn't be able to play against him.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:22.420
But thanks to my old friends, I remembered why I play baseball.

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:26.950
I play baseball simply because I love the game.

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:32.670
I don't need any other reason to play.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:35.880
I see.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.830
Is something wrong?

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:45.300
Well, if you're only playing for fun, then it's no different than backyard baseball.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:51.380
I've counseled many professional athletes in my career,

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:54.730
and they all were in it for more than just fun.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:00.400
They had a strong reason that continually made them strive to be the best.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:05.720
I think you need a reason like that...

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:10.170
if you want to continue to play as a major leaguer.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:17.630
Shigeno.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:22.470
You need a new goal in place of Gibson.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.140
Once you find it,

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:30.060
I think you'll find yourself burning with passion.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.980
A new... goal.

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:46.450
What?!

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:51.660
You haven't gotten in touch with Shigeno even <i>once</i> since he returned to America?

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:52.870
Are you serious?

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.570
Y-Yeah.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:13:00.230
None of my calls go through, and he never calls, obviously.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.150
He doesn't email either.

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:05.800
Why do I have to hear about how he's doing from the news?!

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:09.090
Geez, he's such a moron!

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.210
You're still at it, huh?

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:16.050
You even went to America!

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.310
Don't tell me nothing happened there!

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:23.650
Nothing...

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:29.990
But he's busy trying to get back to the majors, right?

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:34.280
I'm sure he's just too busy to think about his girlfriend.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:37.790
It's not like he'd call if he wasn't busy.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:44.380
I know he's busy, and I'm not desperate for his attention.

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:49.200
I've just been worried about him since I saw that he was demoted.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.220
Suck it up!

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:58.100
How are you going to be the wife of a baseball player if you're already worrying?

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.940
W-Wife?

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.860
Aren't you two going to get married in the future?

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:17.040
M-Marry?

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:21.800
I'm still nineteen and a student.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:22.730
I'm home.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:24.780
Oh, Sis.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:28.300
The news said Shigeno's been reinstated.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:30.800
Really?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.770
Yeah, man...

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:35.430
Looks like we didn't need to worry about his yips—

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:36.850
All right!

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:39.520
Yay!

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.730
Sure, ignore me.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:50.910
Hey, guys!

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:53.490
Yo.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.240
Shigeno, you're back.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.940
Yeah.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.470
You're looking good.

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:01.880
Got your change of pace at the Bats?

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:03.890
Pretty much.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.700
Shigeno!

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:10.600
I've been waiting for you!

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:12.790
H-Hey, stop!

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:15.670
He came back awfully quick.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.430
Think he's fixed?

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:19.730
He technically played fine in the minors,

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:23.490
and the pitches he just threw to me weren't bad.

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:42.570
Oh.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:43.830
You're still here?

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.320
When are you pitching?

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:57.680
They said I'm starting the Titans game in three days.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.800
Against the Titans for your first game back, huh?

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:04.100
They're pretty hard on the pitchers.

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.980
Don't worry.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:16.100
You pitched fine for the Bats, and you got those outs after the run.

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:20.410
You've fully conquered your yips.

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:22.830
Old man.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:28.880
What was your goal in baseball until you retired?

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:32.100
What's this about?

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:34.010
My goal?

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:34.740
Yeah.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:39.190
I was aiming to get to the majors.

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:41.890
Isn't that how it is if you're in the minors?

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:45.330
Why are you asking me something stupid like that?

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:49.190
If you had been promoted to a major league team,

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.610
I wonder what would've happened.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:54.310
Damn it...

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:57.360
How could I have let a nineteen-year-old kid make fun of me?

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:01.180
Yeah, yeah! I wasn't good enough to play in the majors.

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:03.550
That's not what I meant.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:08.900
Well, I don't know everything about being a major leaguer,

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:14.110
but I'm sure you just set a new goal once you get to the majors.

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:15.550
A new goal?

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.880
First would be to stay in the majors.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:22.170
Then to make it onto the starting roster after being a backup.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:27.140
After that, you get more money the better you play.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.650
So basically money's the goal?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.820
Well, what else?

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:35.710
There's nothing wrong with that.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:39.330
You get money and fame from your success.

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.120
You can also give your family a good life.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.790
If you suck, you get fired.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:45.880
That's professional baseball.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:50.590
I see.

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.950
Thanks for your advice.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.300
Shigeno!

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:06.180
Fame and riches, eh?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.800
This could be bad.

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:11.350
I don't care about that at all.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:21.200
We're in the top of the third with the Titans leading 3-1.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.860
With one out and runners on first and third,

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:27.290
the fourth batter, Alex, steps up to the plate.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.110
Shigeno's been brought back to the majors,

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:34.460
but he doesn't seem to have fully recovered.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.020
What's going on?

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:41.540
I brought him back because I thought he was fixed!

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.650
What happened to his sharp pitching?

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:46.020
He should be fine...

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.600
He's only given up a walk so far.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:53.480
I knew we should've given him more time.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.710
A knockout!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:14.290
Shigeno's been knocked out after just three innings!

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:29.710
Maybe...

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:32.110
I'm not cut out for this.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:43.700
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:43.700
<b>Home</b>

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:44.700
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:44.700
<b>Home</b>

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:45.370
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:45.370
<b>Home</b>

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.250
What do you want?

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.790
Hewwo?

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.610
Gowo?

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:54.420
Hey, Chiharu!

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.450
How are you doing?

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:56.280
What's up?

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.080
Need something, Chiharu?

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:59.170
Goro?!

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.680
Me too!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.460
Are you doing all right?

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:04.220
Me want to talk to him too!

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:04.220
We're worried, you know.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.600
You should call from time to time.

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:12.180
Why do we have to find out how you're doing from the news when we're a family?!

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:15.730
Hey, are you listening?!

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:18.010
Yes, I am!

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:19.110
I know!

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:20.190
I already know!

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.370
I'm doing fine!

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:22.270
I see.

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:24.000
W-Well, your father was—

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:25.090
Sure, sure!

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:26.580
See ya.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.020
Goodness!

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:35.330
I didn't get to say what I wanted to!

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:39.250
The game between the Raiders and the Eagles is nearing an end.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:47.120
In the top of the ninth, the Raiders have brought this within one with the score at 5-6 with two outs and bases loaded.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:52.370
Gibson Jr. is at bat, and he's been having some trouble lately.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:57.650
The Eagles' pitcher, Valenzuela, is standing firm on the mound.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:00.430
Now, will Raiders make a huge comeback,

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:03.110
or will they sit back for their seventh straight loss?

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.420
That's the game!

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.250
Gibson Jr. fails for the second time!

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:20.850
He's in a slump.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:27.730
Good.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:29.470
Your pitches are sharp today.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.490
Hey, Keene,

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:33.640
can I have a moment?

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:40.250
Why do I play baseball?

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:45.690
Yeah, I asked Sanders and he said his goal was fame and riches.

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:48.100
It didn't really click with me.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:54.920
I'm wondering how it is for you, as an elite young player.

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:57.170
Why do you ask?

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:00.330
If you choose a job yourself,

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:04.870
it's natural to want to succeed.

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:10.800
Fame and riches just come as part of the package.

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:11.430
As for me,

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:16.980
I just think about how to bat and how to lead before every game I play.

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:20.710
I see.

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:25.690
That sounds more like my style.

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:28.810
I'll stop meaninglessly over thinking it,

00:22:28.810 --> 00:22:33.950
and just focus on winning this game.

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:35.840
Play ball!

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:59.350
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:59.350
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:04.690
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:04.690
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:10.950
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:10.950
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:15.740
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:15.740
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.490 --> 00:23:22.380
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.490 --> 00:23:22.380
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:28.210
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:28.210
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:34.050
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:34.050
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:39.480
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:39.480
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:45.940
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:45.940
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:51.200
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:54.660
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:54.660
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:57.120
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.660 --> 00:24:03.500
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:03.500
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:07.340
sotto

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:07.340
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:15.510
Preview

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:15.510
Preview

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:16.720
I've come back to the major league mound without a new goal.

00:24:17.490 --> 00:24:18.140
I have no choice.

00:24:18.820 --> 00:24:21.900
I'll just have to learn to pitch as a professional.

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:24.400
Next time, on Major: Rookies' Troubles.

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:27.680
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:29.890
Next Time

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:29.890
Next Time

